    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d617">

                <pb facs="0740" n="734" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg734"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/1121a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Henderson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 59</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-13">October 13,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State encloses a certified copy of the protocol in regard to
                    providing the Soviet Union with military supplies, raw materials, equipment and
                    food, signed on October 6, 1942, by Mr. Sumner Welles, Acting Secretary of
                    State, Sir Ronald Campbell, British Minister in Washington, and Mr. Maxim
                    Litvinoff, Ambassador of the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics in
                        Washington.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d617-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Photostats of Annexes II<anchor n="45" xml:id="d617-f2"/> and III<anchor n="46"
                        xml:id="d617-f3"/> are also enclosed and the covering page of Annex
                        I.<anchor n="47" xml:id="d617-f4"/> It is understood that the Embassy has a
                    copy of the body of Annex I.<anchor n="48" xml:id="d617-f5"/>
                </p>
                <p>The texts of the protocol and Annexes are Strictly Confidential and will not be
                    published. Information in regard to their contents should be limited to
                    officials who have duties in relation to their administration.</p>


                <xi:include href="d617-a1.xml" xpointer="d617-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
